  "guards": [
    "The 24-hour clause 17 value is an update-source checking frequency, not an attack, incident or regulator-notification deadline.",
    "The six-month clause 11 retention applies to aggregated information-security events, not every log or raw event.",
    "The six-month clause 23 retention applies only to traffic copies containing attack and/or telecommunications-equipment-control indicators in telecommunications-network PPKA.",
    "The seven-calendar-day clause 25 retention applies to PPKA other than telecommunications-network PPKA and only to traffic copies containing attack indicators.",
    "Do not replace CALENDAR_MONTH with a fixed day count; the order states months.",
    "Intervals selected by a user in clause 11, the inactivity timeout in clause 31 and log retention periods in clause 32 have no prescribed number in Order 554.",
    "Clause 5 does not prohibit all remote administration; it excludes remote control by persons outside the expressly authorized personnel boundary.",
    "Clause 6 requires forced user disable only where manufacturer-provided user-activity monitoring exists.",
    "Order 554 does not state inclusion in a Russian software registry; clause 4 is a legal-entity and foreign-control supply-chain rule.",
    "Detection means and non-telecom PPKA require the specified FSB conformity certificate; cryptographic means must be FSB-certified under their separate clause.",
    "Order 554 contains no special effective-date clause; 2026-01-10 is derived under Decree 763 clause 12 and must not be labeled explicit.",
    "Order 554 replaces Order 196 of 2019; do not apply both as concurrent requirements after the derived effective date."
  ]
